# Fork: minimal upstream conflict

This repository is a fork. Upstream updates must still merge cleanly. Every edit is a patch on someone else's code.

## Do

- Change only the lines required for the task.
- Match the surrounding style, names, and structure, even when a cleaner design exists.
- Prefer a local fix inside the existing method or class over a new abstraction.
- Keep fork-only behavior in the smallest possible place, and mark it with a short comment such as `// fork:` so a later merge can find it.
- Leave unrelated formatting, imports, comments, and file order untouched.

## Do not

- Reformat, rename, move, or reorder code that the task does not require.
- Widen a fix into a refactor, API change, or new layer.
- Touch generated output, build artifacts, or resource files that are not part of the change.
- Replace an upstream pattern with a different one when the existing pattern still works.

```java
// Bad: rename + extract while fixing a null check
public Optional<Item> findListedItem(UUID id) { ... }

// Good: same method, same name, one guarded return
if (item == null) { // fork: skip missing listings during upstream sync
    return;
}
```

If a larger change is the only correct fix, say so before editing and keep the diff as close to upstream as possible.
